# Laravel Conventions (all apps)

Stack: **Laravel 11**, Blade, Livewire 3 (fronts), Filament 3 (hub), Tailwind CSS 4 (fronts).

## Front apps (`arab/`, `china/`)

- `app/Services/HubClient.php`: content GET + leads/events POST; HTTP retry; never call Hub from Blade directly.
- Content path: Hub → **cache** (TTL 5–15 min) → `config/site.php` fallback.
- Leads/events: async best-effort; on failure write local job/log and retry (database queue on the front).
- Livewire MVP: `InvestmentCalculator`, `ContactForm`, `LocaleSwitcher`.
- Sections live in `resources/views/sections/`; keep presentation thin — data from HubClient/config.
- Secrets only in `.env`: `HUB_URL`, `SITE_KEY`, `SITE_SECRET` (or equivalent); never commit tokens.

## Hub

- Version API under `App\Http\Controllers\Api\v1\`.
- Validate/sanitize all lead & event payloads; store `ip_hash`, not raw IP in analytics when hashing is specified.
- Filament resources must respect All/Group/Site scope and role policies.

## Security

- CSRF on web forms; Sanctum token only for server-to-Hub calls (not browser-exposed).
- Rate-limit Hub API; CORS locked to known front origins.
- No shared DB credentials between Hub and promo apps.

## Code style

- Match existing Laravel structure; prefer framework features over custom frameworks.
- Do not add Sanity/Strapi or other CMS in MVP — content is Hub-managed.
- Prefer small, focused changes; don't invent sections/features outside the plan MVP.
